       "text": "I still can't enter this order. The current FDA-approved labeling doesn't support 1600 mg four times daily.\n\n- The prescription ibuprofen label says the total daily dose shouldn't exceed 3,200 mg. This order is 6,400 mg/day.\n- Labeled single doses are 400\u2013800 mg. The label gives 800 mg as the top single dose, and this order is 1,600 mg.\n- OTC labeling is much lower, at 1,200 mg/day.\n\nThe dose is also not an appropriate use of the label, so I won't treat your confirmation as settling it. This would be a possible overdose, and normal kidney and liver function don't remove the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, or cardiovascular events.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum).\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO per day, divided**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you have a specific protocol or a documented indication that justifies the higher dose, you could take it to pharmacy or the attending for review. Order entry would then need to go through whatever override or approval process your institution requires. Tell me which of the doses above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
